00:37:34.765 --> 00:37:37.985
A question that I love
to ask in the hangouts

00:37:39.090 --> 00:37:43.330
it's what's a piece of
career advice that you've received

00:37:43.330 --> 00:37:47.315
or maybe that you've given
that stands out to you?

00:37:47.315 --> 00:37:50.675
Don't know if Jen you
wanna start with this one. Sure.

00:37:50.675 --> 00:37:52.855
So actually mine is, Joe.

00:37:53.395 --> 00:37:55.480
Joe and I just but,
like, here's the go.

00:37:55.480 --> 00:37:58.360
So when I was looking for
my first job, I think Joe, like,

00:37:58.360 --> 00:38:01.000
maybe you and Bella had
this heuristic or something, which

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:05.115
is, like, in any job, you
can really only optimize for two

00:38:05.115 --> 00:38:07.355
things or at least that's like
a way of thinking about it.

00:38:07.355 --> 00:38:09.755
It's like you can only
optimize for two things and everything

00:38:09.755 --> 00:38:12.790
else that you get
is like bonus or or,

00:38:13.350 --> 00:38:15.190
is great that it
comes with a package.

00:38:15.190 --> 00:38:17.830
But once you try to optimize
for more than two things,

00:38:17.830 --> 00:38:19.430
the the equation gets, like,

00:38:19.430 --> 00:38:23.435
very complicated and the the set
of jobs that you can take

00:38:23.435 --> 00:38:27.935
might become too narrow. So an
example is if you care about geography,

00:38:28.790 --> 00:38:31.030
pay, mission, culture,

00:38:32.230 --> 00:38:33.190
growth. You know,

00:38:33.190 --> 00:38:36.150
you can list all these values
that you have and that you want

00:38:36.150 --> 00:38:37.370
out of your next job.

00:38:38.215 --> 00:38:41.655
It probably is like doable
to get something where you're

00:38:41.655 --> 00:38:45.655
mission aligned and get like
a a salary or comp package

00:38:45.655 --> 00:38:46.795
that you're happy with.

00:38:47.310 --> 00:38:50.990
It's probably possible to get a geography
and a comp package that you want.

00:38:50.990 --> 00:38:54.670
It's much harder to try to get
all three in that first job or

00:38:54.670 --> 00:38:56.805
in the current
job that you want.

00:38:56.805 --> 00:39:00.725
And so I really love this
piece of advice because there are a

00:39:00.725 --> 00:39:02.725
couple underlying
principles here.

00:39:02.725 --> 00:39:06.590
One is that it means that you need
to get really clear on what you want.

00:39:06.590 --> 00:39:08.690
Right? And I think
that some people,

00:39:09.310 --> 00:39:12.275
and I fall on this in into
this myself too. It's like,

00:39:12.275 --> 00:39:15.075
people approach you with a
job, you get excited about it,

00:39:15.075 --> 00:39:17.235
